[38;5;231m⏺[39m Added to [38;5;153mindex.html:12[39m:

  - A [38;5;153m<label class="task">[39m wrapping a native [38;5;153m<input type="checkbox">[39m and the item text, so clicking the label toggles
    it.
  - One CSS rule that strikes through the text when checked, giving visible "done" state.

  The checkbox uses the browser's native on/off state — no JS. Not verified in a browser; it's static HTML with no build
  step.

  This was a small, fully specified change, so I implemented it directly rather than running a brainstorming/planning
  workflow. If you want multiple items, persistence, or an add-task form, say the word.

